  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.13.0: UpdateAsync and UpsertAsync delete metadata keys and documents without reading the records first, so two writes of the same record at the same time leave the record of one of them. A collection client chooses once how NullDocumentsDelete deletes a document: WithDocumentCopyKey, or the new WithDocumentDeletionKey and WithEmptyDocumentDeletions; without one, a null document with NullDocumentsDelete throws an ArgumentException, and another way or key throws an InvalidOperationException. On Chroma Cloud, a write with nulls beyond the quota of 32 metadata keys throws an ArgumentException, unless ChromaConfigurationOptions.WithReadsBeyondKeyQuota, and so does a filter on the documents that Chroma Cloud answers with the wrong records: a $regex whose pattern takes an empty text, and a $contains of fewer than 3 characters. An empty text gets an empty BM25 vector. All the releases: https://github.com/ChromaDotNet/ChromaDB.Client/releases. Tested versions: https://github.com/ChromaDotNet/ChromaDB.Client/blob/main/docs/COMPATIBILITY.md. Migration from 1.x: https://github.com/ChromaDotNet/ChromaDB.Client#migrating-from-chromadbclient-1x",
